            <ArticleTitle>New insights into the management of myocardial ischemia. Overview.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>719-21; discussion 743-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Because of their vasodilatory and coronary effects, nitrates are valuable in the treatment of congestive heart failure, acute ischemic syndromes, and stable and unstable angina. Nitrates may also have antiplatelet and antithrombotic effects, and they may prevent adverse remodeling after an acute myocardial infarction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
